 "lessonSteps": [
  {
   "stepId": 1,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/dc28a5af-2c45-402a-81c2-426df7a932f5.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/dc28a5af-2c45-402a-81c2-426df7a932f5_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "In this guide we will work with the OPEN-SMART Serial MP3/WAV player module, which, conveniently, has a built in audio amplifier and comes with a speaker. Start by connecting the speaker to the module using the white molex connector",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Preparing the MP3 Files",
   "stepGroupId": 1
  },
  {
   "stepId": 2,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/e1ae6016-9708-44b6-b0cb-670bef102414.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/e1ae6016-9708-44b6-b0cb-670bef102414_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "Next, we will select the sound files that we wish to play, and upload these files to the micro sd card that we will then insert into the socket on the MP3 module.",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Preparing the MP3 Files",
   "stepGroupId": 1
  },
  {
   "stepId": 3,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/be30b6ed-31ee-4a1b-93b8-8005ff963436.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/be30b6ed-31ee-4a1b-93b8-8005ff963436_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "The player supports 8KHz - 48KHz sampling frequency on MP3 or WAV file formats. Make sure your target files fall under this range. If need be, you can re-sample them using a software such as Audacity, using Open and Export options.",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Preparing the MP3 Files",
   "stepGroupId": 1
  },
  {
   "stepId": 4,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/9db0556e-1e0e-4764-a284-53d6ddb6a0ce.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/9db0556e-1e0e-4764-a284-53d6ddb6a0ce_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "When copying your mp3 or wav files to the micro sd card, place them into folders named 01, 02, 03, ... for the module to be able to access the files.",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Preparing the MP3 Files",
   "stepGroupId": 1
  },
  {
   "stepId": 5,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/4e0df91a-a109-4498-9f6f-6007a521a9a2.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/4e0df91a-a109-4498-9f6f-6007a521a9a2_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "Inside of these folders, name your MP3/WAV files to 3 digit numbers followed by xxx. Eject the card and insert it into the player module",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Preparing the MP3 Files",
   "stepGroupId": 1
  },
  {
   "stepId": 6,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/97144c6e-4963-48ef-ba84-cd425261b3a5.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/97144c6e-4963-48ef-ba84-cd425261b3a5_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "Here, you have 2 options to connect the Serial MP3 module to your microcontroller: Using the Hardware serial connection pins (marked TX, RX) or using Software Serial via almost any 2 pins on the microcontroller. Although Hardware Serial creates a more stable connection especially on ESP8266 boards, it comes at the price of not being able to send messages to the Serial Monitor via serial println commands. Therefore we recommend using Software Serial for Arduino AVR boards and Hardware Serial for ESP8266 boards.",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Hooking up the Module",
   "stepGroupId": 2
  },
  {
   "stepId": 7,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/8aa044ed-1a11-4363-84d4-dc69b21c6983.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/8aa044ed-1a11-4363-84d4-dc69b21c6983_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "Option 1: Hardware Serial. Use the 4-wire serial terminal on your I/O board to connect the Serial Player to the Microcontroller, as in the wiring diagram above",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
   "tips": [],
   "contentTips": [],
   "extraData": {
    "extraDataMaterials": null,
    "extraDataQuestion": null,
    "extraDataForm": null,
    "extraDataTipForm": null
   },
   "stepGroup": "Hooking up the Module",
   "stepGroupId": 2
  },
  {
   "stepId": 8,
   "url": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/5dcd60ca-53e4-4735-8d70-84d68acac13b.jpg",
   "urlTablet": "",
   "urlMobile": "",
   "thumbUrl": "https://d1xhvexl2i3ere.cloudfront.net/makeree/res/5dcd60ca-53e4-4735-8d70-84d68acac13b_thumb.jpg",
   "text": "Option 2: Software Serial. Use the following wiring diagram to connect the Microcontroller to the Serial Player module. Later you may change pin numbers to any available pin, if you need to.",
   "title": "",
   "addToBackground": false,
   "muted": false,
   "autoPlay": false,
   "isGalleryStep": false,
   "isDominantText": false,
   "type": 1,
